Z||000001||V6pack||01-14-2000||02:58 PM||||Great find Fierosound! With injectors too. I'm in Ca. so shipping would kill me and there are still those starter relocation holes to get done and the other mods that would take some $. But...<P>Wish I was living back east after seeing that site!  Been looking out here without seeing those good prices. You could rebuild and still be ahead of the game.<BR>Cool!<BR>V6pack||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||01-14-2000||03:01 PM||||I was at the local Pick'n'Pull yesterday and walked passed about three or four Pontiac/Oldsmobiles that had 3.8L V6 engines in them.  I remember that a couple of them were of the 85/86 vintage (86 Cutlass, I think).  Are these engines any good for swaps if they have to be rebuilt?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||01-14-2000||07:12 PM||||Pass it up if it needs rebuilt. There are plenty of low mileage 3800 V6 engines out there for cheap ($300-$400). Some of the guys I know in the salvage business say these are good, reliable engines, that's why they have so many sitting around in wrecked cars. The ones still in service are still in good condition. A Ford Escort engine is one the salvage yards can't keep in stock because so many people replace them because they wear out or break down a lot.||||reg||1
